---
title: End or restore service, and ACRA updates
description: Archive a client when your firm stops serving it, bring it back, and how ACRA data is kept up to date.
sidebar:
  order: 7
---

## End service for a client

When your firm stops serving a client, end the service. The company is archived; it is not deleted. Managers and tenant admins can do this.

{% steps %}
1. Open the company and select **End service for this client** at the top right.
2. If the company has been struck off, enter the **Struck-off date**. Leave it empty otherwise.
3. Select **End service**.
{% /steps %}

What happens:

- The client is archived and hidden from the companies list (choose **Archived** in **Filter** to see it).
- It no longer counts in annual return figures, filing deadlines and obligation reminders.
- Open cases stay open, and signed agreements keep billing — close or change them separately if needed.
- With a **Struck-off date**: all its officer and shareholder relationships end on that date, and people linked only to this company are archived.

## Restore service

Open the archived company and select **Restore service for this client**. The client comes back to the list. Relationships ended and people archived when the service ended are not restored: add them again if needed.

## Deleting and merging companies

Companies cannot be deleted from Clients, and there is no merge. To stop using a company, end the service. Two companies cannot have the same name or UEN, so duplicates are refused when a company is created.

## ACRA updates

Operon reads ACRA's public company data every week, on Sunday evening Singapore time. For every company with a UEN, it updates:

- the **ACRA company status** (for example Live or Struck off) and the date of the data, shown under **Compliance** on the company page and in the **ACRA status** column of the list;
- the company name, only when it differs from ACRA's in punctuation or spacing.

It never changes your firm's service status, the financial year end or the struck-off date. When ACRA shows a client you still serve as struck off, the company page shows a banner with **End service** so that you can decide.

The weekly update cannot be started from the company page.
